FROM ubuntu
MAINTAINER rohit
RUN apt-get update
CMD ["echo", "Hello From rohit"]

1) Docker -> FROM

- From  instruction set the base image for the dockerfile
- Syntax : FROM <image>:tags
- exp : FROM ubuntu

2) Docker Image Layer 

- docker image consists of the layers
- every single instruction will work like single layer
- FROM will have separe layer, CMD will have separate layer etc....

3) Docker -> RUN

- will run one or more commands in new image layer and commit the result
- syntax : RUN <command>
- exp : 
RUN apt-get update
RUN apt-get install -y vim
 This will add 2 layers

- Recommenmded way is to use multiple commands like one line command
- ex : 
RUN apt-get update && apt-get install -y \
vim \
git

This will add only one layer

4) Docker History

- used to inspect the layres of the image
- Syntax : docker history <image_name>


5) Docker CMD

- used to specify the commands when the container started
- Syntax : CMD["executable(command)", "param1","param2"]
- only one CMD instruction should exists in docker file
- if you add more than one, only the last CMD command will take effect

6) Docker File -> CMD vs RUN

CMD - execute at runtime
RUN - execute at buid time

# More commands

1) docker expose

- Purpose: Documents which port(s) the containerized app listens on.
- ex: EXPOSE 80
- This doesn’t publish the port; it just declares it. You still need -p in docker run to map it.

2) COPY 

- copies files from your host into the image.
- ex: COPY ./app /usr/src/app


3) WORKDIR
- Sets the working directory inside the container for subsequent instructions (RUN, CMD, COPY, etc.).

- ex : WORKDIR /usr/src/app
        COPY . .
        RUN npm install
4) ENV
- Defines environment variables inside the container.
- ex :  ENV PORT=8080
        ENV NODE_ENV=production
5) LABEL

- Adds metadata to your image (key‑value pairs).
- ex :  LABEL maintainer="rohit@example.com"
        LABEL version="1.0"
        LABEL description="My sample app image"


Putting it together

FROM ubuntu:20.04

LABEL maintainer="rohit@example.com"
LABEL version="1.0"
LABEL description="Demo app with Git installed"

WORKDIR /app

ENV DEBIAN_FRONTEND=noninteractive

RUN apt-get update && apt-get install -y git

COPY . .

CMD ["bash"]
